<onlyinclude>A '''code''' is a system of rules that associates symbols, messages or actions with other representations. Morse code represents letters with short and long signals; a computer character code assigns numbers to characters. The term also refers to instructions in programming and to the biological genetic code.

== Explanation ==
Codes may help transmit messages, compress data, detect errors or specify actions. A code is not necessarily secret: encryption uses additional cryptographic rules and keys to protect information. Understanding the code is different from knowing whether a decoded statement is true.

